packCells: initial positions of cells for HemoCell
===================================================

Places cells at random positions and orientations in a box (periodic, or with
walls, or in a pipe) so that their enclosing ellipsoids do not overlap, and
writes one <type>.pos file per cell type for HemoCell's loadParticles().
The user guide describes it in full: doc/user_guide/packcells.rst
(Initial cell positions), including how to pack for the walls of a case.

Build (from the repository root; the binary is tools/packCells/packCells):

  cmake -S tools/packCells -B tools/packCells/build
  cmake --build tools/packCells/build

Examples (sizes in um):

  ./packCells --help
  ./packCells 40 40 40 --hematocrit 0.3 --seed 1
  ./packCells 50 50 98 --hematocrit 0.3 --walls z --offset 0 0 0.75
  ./packCells 51.5 22.9 22.9 --hematocrit 0.3 --cylinder x 11.45 --offset 0 1.55 1.55

Check a packing (Python 3 with numpy; the same box and walls as above):

  python3 check_packing.py 40 40 40 RBC.pos PLT.pos

Credits
-------

The source of this tool uses algorithms and data structures from the work of Monika Bargieł. 
For the original code please visit: https://github.com/malawski/ellipsoids

This tool is created by Gábor Zavodszky from the Computational Science Lab 
in the University of Amsterdam. Any questions or remarks regarding this library 
can be sent to: info@hemocell.eu

## Publications

When using this code, please cite:

1. Bargieł, M., Szczygłowski, Ł., Trzcionkowski, R., Malawski, M., Towards large-scale parallel simulated packings of ellipsoids with OpenMP and HyperFlow, CGW workshop'15 : October 26–28, 2015 Kraków, Poland. Proceedings: eds. Marian Bubak, Michał Turała, Kazimierz Wiatr, Kraków, Academic Computer Centre CYFRONET AGH, 2015. ISBN: 978-83-61433-14-9, 117–118.

2. Bargieł, M., Geometrical properties of simulated packings of ellipsoids, CGW workshop'14 : October 27–29, 2014, Krakow, Poland. Proceedings: eds. Marian Bubak, Michał Turała, Kazimierz Wiatr, Kraków: Academic Computer Centre CYFRONET AGH, 2014. ISBN: 978-83-61433-10-1, 123–124.
